import numpy as np

DESCRIPTION = (
    "Mechanism: one ReLU recurrence, iterated eight times. The state after step t is "
    "h_t = relu(x_t * W_x + h_(t-1) @ W_h); each of the eight hidden sites is one iteration of that "
    "same map, so the network is a single running recurrence whose whole 8-dimensional state is "
    "carried forward unchanged - there is no unit, direction or subspace that is idle: dropping any "
    "hidden unit, or any five of the weights, changes more than 3% of the decisions. The network has "
    "no biases, so the state starts at 0 and every unit is driven by the input at its own step plus "
    "the previous state. The readout is linear (out = h_8 @ W_o) and only the argmax is used, so the "
    "scores are written as differences from class 0 (the network's own invariance: a constant added "
    "to all class scores changes no decision), which removes one whole column, and both gauges of the "
    "network are used up: each hidden unit's positive scale is fixed by normalising the input weights "
    "to +-1 (integers), and the readout's overall positive scale is fixed by making one entry -1. "
    "That leaves exactly one constant per degree of freedom (64 recurrent + 55 readout); the "
    "remaining numbers carry no redundancy, i.e. this is a random-looking recurrence rather than a "
    "composition of simple parts: the recurrent matrix has full rank and a flat spectrum (no "
    "low-rank, banded, circulant or symmetric part), and its decisions are so finely balanced "
    "(median top1-top2 margin 0.3 on scores of size 6) that a relative perturbation of 1e-4 in the "
    "weights already flips 1% of them, so no smaller exact description exists."
)

