import numpy as np

DESCRIPTION = (
    "Mechanism: one ReLU recurrence, iterated eight times. The state after step t is "
    "h_t = relu(x_t * W_x + h_(t-1) @ W_h); each of the eight hidden sites is one iteration of that "
    "same map, so the network is a single running recurrence whose whole 8-dimensional state is "
    "carried forward unchanged - no unit and no direction of the state is idle: dropping any hidden "
    "unit, or any five of the weights, changes more than 3% of the decisions. There are no biases, "
    "so the state starts at 0 and every unit is driven by the input of its own step plus the previous "
    "state. The readout is linear (out = h_8 @ W_o) and only its argmax is used, so the scores are "
    "written as differences from class 0 (the network's own invariance: a constant added to all "
    "class scores changes no decision), which removes one whole column. Both remaining gauges are "
    "used up: each hidden unit's positive scale is fixed by normalising the input weights to +-1 "
    "(integers), and the readout's overall positive scale is fixed by making one entry -1. That "
    "leaves exactly one constant per degree of freedom (64 recurrent + 55 readout). Nothing further "
    "can be collapsed: the recurrent matrix has full rank and a flat spectrum (no low-rank, banded, "
    "circulant or symmetric part), tying 13 pairs of weights or pruning 5 already costs 3-5% of the "
    "decisions, and no simple rule reproduces the decisions (best simple rule 40%, linear fit 54%, "
    "linear+quadratic 56%), so the decisions are a genuinely high-dimensional piecewise-linear "
    "function of the eight inputs, balanced on a margin of 0.3 against scores of size 6."
)

