import numpy as np

DESCRIPTION = (
    "Mechanism: one ReLU recurrence, iterated eight times. Step 1 is degenerate and is written out "
    "explicitly: the first state is relu(x1 * W_x), and since the input weight of every unit is +-1 "
    "in this normalisation, it is a fixed two-ray fan - it holds only the positive and the negative "
    "part of the first input (2 of its 8 coordinates carry independent information): "
    "h1 = relu(x1) * W_plus + relu(-x1) * W_minus, with W_plus / W_minus the positive / negative input "
    "weights (integers). From step 2 on the site is the same map again: "
    "h_t = relu(x_t * W_x + h_(t-1) @ W_h), and the whole 8-dimensional state is carried forward "
    "unchanged - no unit and no direction is idle (dropping a hidden unit destroys the decisions, "
    "zeroing five weights costs 3%). The readout is linear and only its argmax is used, so the scores "
    "are written as differences from class 0 (the network's own invariance: a constant added to all "
    "class scores changes no decision), which removes one whole column; each hidden unit's positive "
    "scale is fixed by normalising the input weights to +-1, and the readout's overall positive scale "
    "by making one entry -1. That leaves exactly one constant per degree of freedom (64 recurrent + "
    "55 readout). Nothing further collapses: the recurrent matrix has full rank and a flat spectrum "
    "(no low-rank, banded, circulant or symmetric part), equating 13 pairs of weights already costs "
    "5% of the decisions and breaks the intermediate states, and no simple rule reproduces the "
    "decisions (best simple rule 40%, linear fit 54%, linear+quadratic 56%), so they are a "
    "high-dimensional piecewise-linear function of the eight inputs balanced on a margin of 0.3 "
    "against scores of size 6."
)

